===================================================

No licence has been selected yet. Without an explicit licence, default
copyright applies and others cannot legally reuse this code.

Before making this repository public, replace this file with a licence of
your choice. Common options for research code:

  - MIT          : very permissive, minimal conditions
  - Apache-2.0   : permissive, includes an explicit patent grant
  - GPL-3.0      : copyleft, derivatives must stay open

GitHub can add any of these for you: in the repo, click "Add file" ->
"Create new file", name it LICENSE, and GitHub offers a licence picker.

SEPARATE NOTE ON THE DATA:
The files under data/ are a screening database referencing third-party
publications. The coding/extraction is your work; the underlying papers are
not. Consider adding a short data-use statement, and check any requirements
from Lancaster University and from journals where related chapters may be
published. (This is not legal advice.)

